Patch 13 -- p70 ABI-admitted draw-state phase-A correctness bridge.

Incremental after patch 12 and Wine patch 67. Entry 40 carries one pointer to a
guest-stack argument object and invokes only the contiguous resource/stream
preload transaction after the guest has acquired and made the GL context
current. Guest x86 retains context_apply_draw_state() control flow, phases
B/C/D, final submission, barriers and release.

MGS2_PHASE_A_CORRECTNESS enables a seven-word exported memory-only record for
calls and guest fallbacks. It adds no stderr output and is intended only for the
first correctness run. The wrapper reuses the p67 TLS guard and fails closed to
the guest body when the guard is unavailable.

Regenerate mgs2_island_entry_identity.h and class B from the exact paired p70
DLL. The device artifact has entry 40 marker +29 at canonical RVA 0xb9410 and
1,616 class-B IDs. This patch makes no frame-rate claim.

